Timothy force looks to major in English  and minor in economics in Latin he has a  3.6 for grade point average his future  plans include business ownership and  farming on campus he volunteers for a  few good men belongs to the Catholic  society and works as a house director in  the Suites he also plays on the club  soccer team beside his campus activities  he assists with a youth ministry at the  st. anthony catholic church he  previously belonged to the Boy Scouts  where he reached the rank of Eagle Tim  is the third of four children his  younger brother is a post-secondary  student the family resides in Colorado  Springs Colorado his father is employed  employed in sales and his mother is  self-employed thank you dr. Whelan Thank  You Larissa I would also like to thank  grounds and maintenance for this  wonderful set up on the east lawn and  finally I'd like to thank the college's  horticulturalist Angie for the work she  does for this school including the  arrangements you see here today I am  truly humbled to speak before all of you  today but I would like to spare you any  sort of congratulations you already know  that you have the envy of all your dad's  friends who watch conservative talk  radio and I already know that you know  that Hillsdale is the best college in  the nation for goodness sakes if the  trend is continuing then you are the  most intelligent class at this school  has ever admitted which means that you  had options lots of options and yet you  are sitting here so in lieu of  congratulations congratulating you for  something that you already know is a  spectacular accomplishment I would like  to simply share with you the single most  formative thing that I have learned  during my time here this important  lesson had like most important lessons  been a lifetime in the making but the  most crucial steps were not taken into  my own freshman convocation the day that  I entrusted my education in the liberal  arts to Hillsdale College my freshman  year far exceeded my expectations my  high school senior bravado was certainly  knocked down a couple notches by  rigorous academics and my increased  independence showed me that my parents  had done much more for me than I had  ever known despite these couple of tough  realizations my first semester here at  Hillsdale pushed me to a before unknown  level  of intellectual activity dr. Cal Toph  made his western heritage class consider  the nature of the well-ordered life dr.  gaetano gave his American heritage class  way too much information about the  private life of William Byrd and he  warned us about the dangerous ideas of  those who wish to imitate eyes the  eschaton I cannot wait for you all to  understand what I just alluded to and  dr. Linley showed his great books class  that Polyphemus the Cyclops is not  simply one of Homer's mythical creatures  but also a lesson to readers that we  have two eyes for a reason and the  perspective provided by these two eyes  should not be wasted I somewhat  mistakenly believe that coming to  understand these ideas was the sole  reason I attended this prestigious  academic institution it was not into my  sophomore year and one of dr. she  leaders philosophy classes that a single  sentence showed me that Hillsdale was  offering me much more if only I would  let it the sentence comes from an  incredible 1965 document called gaudiya  med spez which translates from the Latin  into joy and hope it's a lovely title  the sentence reads man who is the only  creature on earth which God willed for  itself cannot fully find himself except  through a sincere gift of himself I am  not equipped to dissect all the  intricacies of this statement plus I do  not want to burden you with a lengthy  digression but I can tell you that it  was largely this statement that formed  the man standing before you today if I  may I would like to dial back the  philosophical tenure of the sentence and  paraphrase it as a human being due to  his likeness to God is unlike any other  created thing and therefore does not  fully become a human being until he can  selflessly give himself to something  other than himself naturally I needed to  take this paraphrase one step further  and read the sentence as I Tim Force  profoundly and beautifully resemble my  Creator in order to become what my  Creator intended me to be I must fully  submit my life to things and people  other than myself I might just be a nerd  but seriously this changes everything  first of all it radically altered my  perception of hillsdale's liberal arts  education I discovered that the reality  of the liberal arts is not contained in  Lane Kendall Stroh Sakura dau but rather  the classroom simply provides us with  the raw materials with which we can  fully understand ourselves it is then  our responsibility to steward these raw  materials and by means of conversation  and reflective thought learn who we are  and who we ought to be once we come to a  fuller understanding of ourselves then  we can willingly and holistically give  our lives to other people or pursuits  secondly this lesson I learned about  giving myself to other change the way I  perceive hardship I'm not going to  sugarcoat this when the last couple of  weeks of each semester roll around you  will be tired you will be homesick and  you will probably wonder why you  willingly pay for the end of the  semester abuse having felt all those  feelings six times I can tell you that  it was that what I was feeling was  really just cleverly disguised egoism  and those closing weeks of the semester  I'm prone to forget that my primary  concern should not be my GPA my  reputation and my desire to get home  rather I should strive to be fully  myself and to do this I must recommit  myself to giving my life to the higher  calling of education to my close friends  who continually give their lives to me  to my parents who simply want to know  that they are loved and appreciated and  to all the other people who I should be  treating as neighbors I promise you that  this is easier said than done but if on  a daily basis you can sincerely recommit  yourself to those people and purposes  then your egoism will not fuel your  self-pity during those difficult  situations I feel inclined to warn you  that this sort of radical gift of self  is not always possible by human means  alone so I implore you to nurture a  vibrant prayer life a prayer life in  which you can give yourself to divine  and with which you can ask God for the  graces to give yourself to other people  and purposes I would now like to cite  three concrete examples of the joy and  fulfillment of a life lived for others  my first example comes from an  experience I had early in my freshman  year one night after a particularly  disheartening attempt to write a paper  in the old student union lab I started a  dejected 3am walk back to Simpson 1fn I  intended to Walla winsome self-pity  before getting some well need  sleep but my hallmate you I West had a  different idea Eli saw my vulnerability  and other than exploiting it he decided  to share his own vulnerabilities only  God knows why he was awake at that  horrible hour but instead of focusing on  his own troubles he gifted his life to  me by means of a short prayer and his  time Eli taught me a critical lesson  about self gift that night and for that  he should be giving this speech but at  the very least find him and if you live  on his Hall in Simpson you have an  invaluable friend my second example  comes from my sophomore roommate Tyler  Wilkie the men of need filled  endearingly called him Haas which was  fitting because he practically sweat  self gift almost every weekend he would  make the five hour trip to his family's  farm in northern Illinois ten cattle and  harvest crops for two days start his  homework around eleven o'clock Sunday  night and amazingly be prepared for  class on Monday if that is not enough he  helped build sets for the drama  department and was a key volunteer in a  few good men he even went so far as to  how haul a plow truck from his farm to  Hillsdale and he enlisted me to  voluntarily plow ten driveways any time  it snowed that is a big commitment in  south central michigan you might be  saying that it does not sound like  academics or his top priority and you  would be right he put much before his  school work yet as we speak he is  working through his second year at drake  law school Tyler Wilkie taught me how  that somehow it is possible to never be  too busy to give yourself to others my  third example comes from a very recent  experience come next Sunday my wife and  I will have shared three full and happy  months of marriage that sentence from  Gowdy Emmett's bez truly came into focus  as I stood with her before the altar and  now every day I enjoy her gift of self  to me and I get to continually practice  giving myself to her I can tell you with  certainty that the most important date  in the last four years of my life will  not be my first or last day here at  Hillsdale but rather June 4th the day  that Perry Rose taught me the full  meaning of that powerful sentence from  gaudiya meds bez I thank all of you for  your time and your decision to join in  the partnership of hillsdale college I  would like to leave you with this the  best gift that you can give this  institution and certainly the best gift  that you can give any person is your  unreserved and through  see astok and joyful self thank you and  good luck
 

